---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Cristian Serrano - Digital Product Designer"
  description="Cristian Serrano is a Senior Product Designer and Design Systems specialist with 17+ years of experience, based in Munich. Focused on making the complex simple."
>
  <section id="hero">
    <h1 class="hero-title">Hi! I'm Cristian :) </h1>
    <p class="blog-lead-paragraph">I'm a digital product designer with <span id="experienceYears"></span> of experience who enjoys the challenge of making the complex simple.</p>
    <p class="blog-lead-paragraph">But surely you already know that from <a href="/cv">my CV</a>, or <a target="_blank" href="http://www.linkedin.com/in/cristianserrano">my LinkedIn</a>; let's jump into more interesting stuff you probably don't know about me.</p>
  </section>

  <hr class="bold-divider">

  <section id="about-me">

    <h2 class="blog-text-2">So, about me</h2>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="smiling face with glasses">🤓</span> I'm curiosity-driven.</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">Design isn't just my job, my role, or something that I'm good at. Being a designer is something that I just am, it's about the way I see the world. I'm curious by nature and I often find myself thinking about how everything around me works, and how can I make it better.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="glowing star"> 🌟</span> I'm always learning</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">Curiosity leads to discoveries. And discoveries lead to learning. Well, hopefully. =P Learning opens your mind, and retrofeeds curiosity. And then, as time goes by, you end up with this breadth of skills and abilities and interests and there's only so much time to do everything. But that's ok, you're a <a href="https://airbnb.design/defining-design-generalists/" target="_blank">Generalist</a> now; welcome to the big picture. ;)</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="blue heart">🌼</span> I'm actively seeking new opportunities</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">Designing impactful, people-centered experiences is my focus, and I'm excited about what's next. I'm on the lookout for a role where I can bring my experience in product and systems design to a team that values curiosity, autonomy, and innovation. I'm ready to deep dive into meaningful projects that make a real difference—let's create something great together!</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="party popper">🎉</span> I celebrate Mondays</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">I get the people looking forward to the weekend because they can't wait to get away from their jobs. Now, don't get me wrong: I enjoy the weekends as much as the next person, but I love what I do. I look forward to Mondays to come back to work, team up with talented people, and do great stuff even greater.</p>
    </article>

  </section>

  <section id="about-you">

    <h2 class="blog-text-2">Nice! How about you?</h2>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="house with garden">🏡 </span>You're looking for an in-house seasoned product designer</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">Having worked in startups, agencies, and also with clients as a freelancer, I've found that I do my best work as an in-house designer. I look forward to being part of a strong Design team, having ownership of the design process, and being there to see the product –and the team– grow. I'm also looking for a place where I can grow into a <a href="https://shareg.pt/fhENdee" target="_blank">Design Operations</a> role.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="gold medal">🥇 </span>You strive for an awesome culture of work</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">Context shapes us, and we shape the products we build. You believe that in <span class="current-year"></span> a successful company should be like a diverse, caring, fun, playful, and hard-working community. That kind of nurturing workplace can only lead to great relationships, and great relationships lead to great products. :)</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="money bag">💰 </span>You value the work being put into your products</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">Ideally, you advocate for salary transparency; you find it ethical and practical as well. At the very least, you don't encourage salary secrecy and don't mind your employees talking about it because everyone is paid fairly for their efforts. Plus, you know that this enables your employees to have an overall better quality of life and they can focus on doing good work, instead of having to spend time lobbying for their compensation.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="world map">🗺️ </span>You embrace remote and hybrid working</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">You understand the benefits of allowing employees a flexible schedule. After having experienced on-site positions, as well as hybrid and fully remote ones, I've found that while I can keep my productivity up while working from home, I do miss going every now and then to the office and spending quality time with my teammates. Also, for specific topics like hackathons or Design Sprints, it's very valuable to have a more personal approach.</p>
    </article>

  </section>

  <section id="why-me">

    <h2 class="blog-text-2">What do I bring to the table?</h2>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="diamond">💎 </span>Resiliency</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">Born and raised in Argentina, where there's always a crisis at hand, we live our day-by-day dealing with uncertainty. We are forced to adapt and reinvent ourselves to find opportunities to grow; we even have a word for it: Opportuncrisis. I like to think about it as kind of a cultural trait: we develop resilience to high-uncertainty contexts.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="gear">⚙️ </span>Systems-oriented thinking</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">I see product design (and development, for that matter) holistically, with the whole being greater than the sum of its parts, and everything being deeply interconnected. I'm convinced that good design/development is scalable, and scalability needs systems and logic thinking.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="wave">🌊 </span>Adaptability</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">Being a fast learner (and, why not, unlearner =P) is one of my strengths. I welcome feedback to iterate myself and, though I prefer to work smart, I can roll up my sleeves and work hard when it's needed. I'm comfortable staying on the path as well as exploring wildly. I love bouncing ideas with other people, but I can do great work on my own as well, and I'm not afraid challenging the status quo when I feel a change is needed. ;)</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3 class="blog-text-3"><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="flexed biceps">🚀 </span>Team player mindset</h3>
      <p class="blog-paragraph">We all know the go-to phrases about teamwork: "If you want to go fast, go alone. If you want to go far, go together.", "The whole is greater than the sum of its parts.", and so on. I know they might sound a bit cheesy, but I genuinely believe them to be true. No one alone can make a difference, together we divide our weaknesses and together we multiply our strengths.</p>
    </article>

  </section>

  <hr class="bold-divider">

  <section id="cta">
    <h2 class="blog-text-2">Awesome! What now?</h2>
    <p class="blog-paragraph">Alright! If you've made it this far, then sorry about the length :P and thanks! It means that most probably you're interested in my profile and that's a huge deal for me! <span class="emoji-end" role="img" aria-label="party popper">🎉</span></p>
    <p class="blog-paragraph">If that's the case, then I guess you might want to take a look at <a class="inline" href="/work">some of my work</a> next and possibly contact me, so <a href="/contact">here's how.</a></p>
    <p class="blog-paragraph">If it's not, then... uhmm... this is a little awkward.<span class="emoji-end" role="img" aria-label="grimacing face">😬</span></p>
    <p class="blog-paragraph">Either way, thanks a lot for your time and I hope you have a great day.</p>
    <p class="blog-paragraph">Cheers!<span class="emoji-end" role="img" aria-label="waving-hand">👋🏼</span></p>
  </section>
</Layout>
